# Finish the canonical `src/<domain>/<function>/<kind>/<part>` migration

Finish the canonical `src/<domain>/<function>/<kind>/<part>` migration.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Finish the canonical `src/<domain>/<function>/<kind>/<part>` migration.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

Canonical product source now has five explicit domains: `formats`, `foundation`,
`localization`, `migration`, and `unreal`. Every domain owns `README.md` plus
`shar-boundary/v1` metadata, and every immediate function directory owns a
`shar-function/v1` record declaring the canonical
`src/<domain>/<function>/<kind>/<part>` route.

The language-mod implementation moved from the noncanonical `src/languages/`
root to `src/localization/languages/` without changing its Rust package API.
Metadata for `json-text`, `sha256`, and `asset-conversion` was corrected to
include the physical `composition` kind that already existed.

Architecture tests now fail if a domain lacks boundary metadata, a function lacks
`function.yml`, identity domain/path diverges from the filesystem, the canonical
route changes, or declared kinds differ from physical nonlocal kind directories.
The current audit covers all five domains and 16 functions; the moved language
crate retains all nine localization tests.